# AGENTS.md

## Repository purpose

`mcp-{name}` is an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server that {description}.

## Common commands

```bash
python -m venv venv
source venv/bin/activate
pip install -e ".[dev]"
python -m mcp_{name_underscore}.server
pytest
ruff check .
ruff format --check .
```

## Project conventions

- Target Python 3.11 or newer.
- Keep protocol traffic on stdout only. Use logging configured for stderr and
  never call `print` from a stdio MCP server.
- Validate required configuration without logging credential values.
- Keep external API access behind a focused client module and test it with
  mocked responses.
- Before opening a change, run the test suite and Ruff checks.

## Layout

```text
src/mcp_{name_underscore}/server.py  MCP server entry point
tests/                               Unit and integration tests
server.json                          MCP Registry metadata
```

## Releases

Python releases are tag-driven, not managed by Release Please. Create and push
a version tag such as `v1.2.3` to trigger the release workflow and publish to
PyPI.
